Viewer: auto resolution goes up to 2560 on the long side once the browser decodes fast (2026-10-19).

Auto took the screen's real pixels but stopped at 1920, so a 2.5K screen got 1920 scaled up while owners set
2560 by hand. With a fast decoder (the same gate as real pixels and H.265) the cap is now 2560; a slow decoder
keeps 1920. A Tesla's 1920x1200 panel and the XPeng (about 1533 wide) ask for what they did before.

